--TEST--
`prepareRename` inside a string is refused even where the text spells a class's name, because a string's contents are no symbol, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class User
{
    public string $name = "";
}

echo "Us<|>er";
--REQUEST--
prepareRename
--EXPECT--
refused: There is nothing to rename here. You can rename a class, a variable, a method, a property, a constant or an enum case.
